    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver: this decides trip TRP-02722. The SGD 4.50 cancellation fee charged to the rider is refunded in full, and no payment is made to the driver.\n\nWHY THE FEE DOES NOT STAND. POL-NS-01 charges a no-show fee only if all four of its limbs hold. Limb (b) requires the GPS trace to place the driver inside the pickup geofence, and limb (c) requires a continuous in-geofence dwell of at least the free waiting period in force — 180 seconds here (EV-TRIP-02722, platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180). The driver's trace EV-GPS-02722 is complete and clean (100 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps, weight_multiplier 1.0), and its derived arrival block reports 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes and a longest qualifying run of 0.0 seconds. Under POL-NS-02 the driver is therefore deemed not to have arrived, limb (b) fails, and under POL-NS-06 the effective dwell of 0 seconds falls 180 seconds short of the free waiting period (shortfall_sec 180.0). The cancellation-fee line of SGD 4.50 (EV-FARE-02722, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) is refunded in full. POL-NS-06 requires that refund whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider answered messages.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S CASE, ANSWERED. The 'I'm Here' tap at 19:11:37 and the driver's cancellation at 19:18:19 under RIDER_NO_SHOW do establish limbs (a) and (d), and the driver is right that the trace carries no POL-NS-08 defect — which is precisely why the absence finding is real and not the product of a gappy export. But all four limbs are required. The submission that the trace's minimum distance of 0.0 m shows the driver reached the pin is rejected: POL-NS-02's test reads consecutive fixes with reported accuracy of 25 m or better inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, and the trace yields none; a trace-wide minimum distance is not that test, and the driver's own advocate concedes the exported trace does not establish the dwell. The reliance on POL-NS-12 fails on that clause's own terms: it covers only a platform-confirmed GPS_AUTO arrival, and this trip's arrival_marker is BUTTON — a driver-pressed marker, which POL-NS-12 expressly excludes; the wait-timer event therefore cannot stand in for the geofence measurement. The message 'im at the pickup point' at 19:11:57 (EV-CHAT-02722) shows the driver coordinating, but it is his own assertion and does not meet the arrival test. The counterparty statement 'I was at the pin for over six minutes' is an account with no weight_multiplier; it neither carries the arrival fact nor moves the confidence cap. POL-NS-07 compensation therefore does not arise (the computed SGD 3.60 is not payable), and in any event the anti-farming check does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d 1 against completed_trips_30d 130 is a rate of 0.0077, below the 0.08 threshold and below the count of 4. POL-NS-03 goodwill of SGD 2.25 is also not payable: registered_pickup_points is 1, so the pin-ambiguity limb (which needs 2 or more) is not engaged, and no stationary dwell within 400 m of the pin is established.\n\nTHE RIDER'S CASE, ANSWERED. The driver is correct that the rider's own track (75 fixes, all at 0.0 kph) sits about 895 m from the pin throughout and that rider_qualifying_fix_count is 0; the rider was not at the pickup point. That does not change the fee outcome, which POL-NS-06 gives regardless of rider presence, and POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider on the contact limb because the rider sent no message. The submission that the arrival marker is FALSE under POL-NS-05, with a false-arrival referral, is rejected: no derived fact matches a GPS fix to the 19:11:37 timestamp, and trip-wide speeds of up to 62.8 km/h do not establish the driver's speed at the marker. That makes no difference to the money — the refund follows from POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06 independently — and no clause therefore produces a referral. The rider's disclosure about EV-ADVIS-02722-01 is correct: it is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), so POL-NS-06(i) accumulation is unavailable; the missing artifact carries no fact and is not part of the confidence cap.\n\nCONFIDENCE AND WEIGHT. The ruling rests on EV-GPS-02722 and EV-TRIP-02722, each at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and no deciding artifact is discounted. Confidence is 0.85.\n\nEXECUTION AND APPEAL. The monetary effect, SGD 4.50, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold (POL-GEN-05), so it executes automatically on issue. This ruling was made without human review and is provisional; either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04.\n\nOPEN QUESTION FOR THE RECORD. The driver's track reports a minimum distance of 0.0 m to the pin, which the qualifying-fix test cannot reconcile with a zero-second in-geofence run; the platform's full-resolution stream would settle it. It does not change this outcome, which follows from POL-NS-02 as the exported trace stands."
