    "explanation": "The SGD 4.50 cancellation fee charged on the 18 August trip is refunded to the rider in full. The driver receives no compensation.\n\nWhy the fee does not stand. POL-NS-01 allows a no-show fee only if all four of its conditions hold. Conditions (a) and (d) are met: the trip record shows the driver's 'I'm Here' tap at 19:11:37, and the trip was terminated at 19:18:19 with no boarding and reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW. Conditions (b) and (c) are not met. Under POL-NS-02 a driver is deemed to have arrived only if the GPS trace holds at least three consecutive fixes, each accurate to 25 m or better, inside the 50 m arrival radius for a STANDARD pickup. The trace (EV-GPS-02722) computes zero qualifying in-geofence fixes and a longest qualifying run of 0.0 seconds. That trace is clean — 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps and no clock skew — so the absence of a qualifying arrival is a real finding, not the product of a sparse export. Condition (c) needs a continuous dwell of at least the free waiting period in force, 180 seconds, read from trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec. The measured dwell is 0.0 seconds: a 180-second shortfall. POL-NS-06 therefore makes the fee unchargeable and refunds it in full, whether or not the rider was present.\n\nAnswering the driver. The platform wait-timer argument is rejected. POL-NS-12 makes the platform's arrival and wait-timer events an independent carrier only where arrival_marker is GPS_AUTO; this trip's marker is BUTTON. An arrival tap set by the driver records only that he tapped it, and POL-NS-01(c) measures the dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, not from the tap. The argument from the trace's minimum distance of 0.0 m is rejected: the derived arrival computation is authoritative and reports no in-geofence interval in which the driver held position, so passing over the pin is not holding at it. POL-NS-03 does not apply: there is no stationary dwell outside the arrival radius but within 400 m, and with one registered pickup point (registered_pickup_points = 1) its pin-ambiguity limb cannot be reached, so no goodwill or driver compensation arises. The driver's own concession that the exported trace does not itself establish the dwell is correct, but it does not save the fee, because POL-NS-12 is unavailable and no other carrier supports the wait. POL-NS-07 compensation is not payable: it operates only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it does not. In any event the anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d = 1 against completed_trips_30d = 130, a rate of 0.008). The anti-escalation points on both profiles are accepted.\n\nAnswering the rider. Accepted: that there is no qualifying in-geofence fix (POL-NS-02); that the dwell shortfall is 180 seconds against the 180-second free waiting period (POL-NS-06); that the GPS export is complete so the absence of arrival is genuine; that the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02722-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0 and issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, so POL-NS-06(i) accumulation is unavailable and no advisory carries any fact; that the fare line of SGD 4.50 reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of 4.50, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect; and that neither profile raises a POL-NS-09(c) or (d) ground. The rider's claim that the rider's own track shows the rider waiting at the pin is only partly right: the device was stationary, but at roughly 895 m from the pin (mean 895.2 m, min 891.7 m, 0 qualifying fixes), outside the 100 m presence radius, so POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider and POL-NS-11 does not arise. That does not change the refund, which POL-NS-06 gives whether or not the rider was present. The request for a POL-NS-05(ii) false-arrival referral is not granted: that limb fires only after the arrival marker is itself found false, which requires the driver's distance (over 300 m) or speed (15 km/h or more) at 19:11:37, and the record fixes neither. POL-NS-05 therefore cannot be run on this record and no clause produces a referral; the point is left here as an observation for the reader, not an instruction.\n\nConfidence and next steps. The deciding fact — the driver's failure to establish the required in-geofence dwell — is carried by EV-GPS-02722 at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0 and confidence is set at 0.88. No POL-NS-09 trigger is engaged (confidence is above the 0.70 floor, the two records do not contradict each other on a fact no clause resolves, the counterparty-dispute counters are zero, the anti-farming check does not trip, and the deciding evidence is not impaired). The monetary effect, SGD 4.50, is below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold, so it executes on issue. Both parties may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
