outside the radius but within 400 m, and the trace shows no in-geofence holding interval (longest qualifying run 0.0 s); in any event this pickup has 1 registered pickup point, so the pin-ambiguity goodwill limb could not apply. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 1 against completed_trips_30d 130, a rate of 0.008, below both the count of 4 and the rate of 0.08), so no escalation is triggered and compensation would have been payable had the fee stood; it does not stand.\n\nRider. Your POL-NS-04 exoneration is not needed and does not run: your own device track sits about 892 m from the pickup pin throughout (min 891.7 m, mean 895.2 m, 75 fixes), so limb (c) fails and the clause cannot exonerate you — the refund rests on the driver's evidence, not on your presence. I also decline a POL-NS-05(ii) false-arrival referral: that limb runs only where the trace places the driver more than 300 m from the pin, or in motion at 15 km/h or above, at the arrival timestamp, and the record reports neither figure for 19:11:37. The marker is uncorroborated and carries nothing, but an unresolved question about it is not a clause-mandated referral. The MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02722-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact and is not relied on by either side; the driver's claim about it was discarded for non-disclosure of the impairment and appears in the discarded list. Neither profile-based escalation ground is engaged (no_show_disputes_30d 0, disputes_with_counterparty_90d 0 on both sides).\n\nNo artifact this ruling rests on is below full weight (trip record and GPS trace are both complete at weight 1.0), so the POL-GEN-02 confidence cap is 1.0. The monetary effect, SGD 4.50, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so the refund executes on issue."
